WEBVTT

00:00:03.100 --> 00:00:06.270
Before we dive in, let’s look at the whole picture.

00:00:06.320 --> 00:00:12.170
The six conversations are: Why are we here? Who are we? How do we work?

00:00:12.220 --> 00:00:13.990
How do we make decisions?

00:00:14.040 --> 00:00:15.830
How do we want to be together?

00:00:15.880 --> 00:00:18.130
And how do we learn and reform?

00:00:18.180 --> 00:00:20.650
You can think of them in three pairs.

00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:27.510
Why and Who are about identity: the purpose that holds you together, and the people who make up the team.

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:33.450
Rhythm and Decisions are about operating: how work flows, and how choices get made.

00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:39.870
Values and Evolve are about culture and time: how you treat each other, and how you keep improving.

00:00:39.920 --> 00:00:41.650
There is no fixed order.

00:00:41.700 --> 00:00:46.730
A brand-new team usually starts with Why and Who, because everything else rests on them.

00:00:46.780 --> 00:00:52.790
But a team that’s been together for years and keeps reopening decisions should probably start with Decisions.

00:00:52.840 --> 00:00:55.550
A team in conflict might start with Values.

00:00:55.600 --> 00:00:58.750
Start where it hurts, or where the energy is.

00:00:58.800 --> 00:01:01.850
Each conversation follows the same simple pattern.

00:01:01.900 --> 00:01:04.170
A few key questions open it up.

00:01:04.220 --> 00:01:07.630
One exercise gives the team a structure to think and talk.

00:01:07.680 --> 00:01:12.670
And the result is written down on the team canvas, so it doesn’t evaporate after the session.

00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:15.230
That last part matters more than it sounds.

00:01:15.280 --> 00:01:17.370
Most teams have good conversations.

00:01:17.420 --> 00:01:20.990
Few teams capture what they agreed in a way they come back to.

00:01:21.040 --> 00:01:24.030
The canvas is your team’s shared memory.

00:01:24.080 --> 00:01:32.350
If you’re not sure where to start, the two-minute team health check on formyourteam.dk will point you to the conversation your team needs most.

00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:34.925
It’s a good thing to do with your team before your first session.

